@startuml

title The scheduled job and the firings it records

class "job\n(job definition)" as job <<configuration>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +job name : name
    {field} +schedule expression : cron expression
    {field} +action kind : name
    {field} +action material : text
    {field} +tenant : tenant id, or none for a system job
    {field} +party : party id, or none
    {field} +active : flag
}

class "firing\n(job instance)" as firing <<state>> #FFF4E1 {
    {field} +job : job definition id
    {field} +action kind : name
    {field} +triggered at : instant
    {field} +started at : instant
    {field} +completed at : instant, or none
    {field} +duration : milliseconds, or none
    {field} +state : starting | succeeded | failed
    {field} +reason : text
}

job "1" --> "*" firing : records

note bottom of job
    Configuration: it defines when the job runs
    and what the firing does. A change affects
    later firings, not earlier ones.
end note

note bottom of firing
    State: one execution, recorded before its
    action starts. The reason is stored when
    the state is failed.
end note

@enduml
